Restore Wayland 1.0.3's return-after-read behavior for the untimed dispatch APIs.

QtWayland 5.0 selects the display fd before dispatching its default queue.
A read containing only Mesa EGL-queue events must be allowed to return zero;
otherwise WAM polls again forever and cannot answer QtWebProcess's sync IPC.
Keep both timeout APIs (including a NULL timeout) on the modern behavior.
The first read still blocks; pending events, read coordination and errors retain
upstream handling. Roundtrip/EGL callers already loop until their callback fires.

